  "reported_status": "The campaign reports an angle-independent rank bound for uniform states on ranges of injective maps sharing a domain, plus a conditional guarded-history construction whose success bound requires acquired recurrence, decoder and chart structure. Neither result supplies the general polynomial-cost encoder. The Bell-projector normalization counterexample rejects a proposed shortcut. No historic breakthrough is established.",
  "scientific_scope_status": "For injective M,N on the same r-dimensional domain, the reported trace-distance bound compares normalized uniform range states and is at most rank(M-N)/r. Its graph truncation application controls selected range states, not the output of the map on a uniform logical input. A separate history-lift bound is conditional on bounded branch count/contraction, an acquired common decoder and orthogonal logical chart block, and exact recurrence; missing acquisition, normalization, consistency and disconnected composition prevent an end-to-end general encoder. Finite rational diagnostics do not certify the universal claims.",
  "status_authority": "User-provided campaign continuation and report/source preservation; no scientific execution or proof reconstruction.",
